{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/954940-hack-2nd-edition-mockeries","id":954940,"title":"[Hack] 2nd edition Mockeries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-21T07:25:04-07:00","id":954940,"title":"[Hack] 2nd edition Mockeries","content":"I very much enjoyed the Mockeries of 1st edition, and intend to keep them in crossovers/future campaigns. As a setting 'hack', it's as simple as just re-introducing them as the five (or more) categories of Pandorans mirroring the lineages. System wise, here's what I intend to use:<br /> <br /> Ishtari: the Mockeries of the Tammuz are patient hunters who enjoy trapping and slowly consuming Prometherans.<br /> All Ishtari gain the Inertia Dread Power (see below). Additionally, they require to be exposed to Azothic radiance for a full scene, rather than one minute, before awakening.<br /> <br /> Renders: the Mockeries of the Ulgan and fast and lethal, seeking to tear apart the flesh of their preys.<br /> All Renders gain the Bizarre Weaponry (2) and Scurry (2) Dread Powers. Additionally, they are always considered Open for spirits and ghosts to influence them.<br /> <br /> Sebek: the ravenous Mockeries of the Nepri seek to devour Prometheans in their watery lairs.<br /> All Sebek gain the Armor (1), Bizarre Weaponry (2), and Beastly Mutation (1) Dread Powers, the later representing their ability to breathe under water. Additionally, they must succeed at a Resolve+Composure roll penalized by the target's Azoth to stop attacking a Promethean from whom they have tasted the flesh.<br /> <br /> Silent Ones: gliding silently on leathery wings, the Silent Ones hate beauty over all things.<br /> All Silent Ones gain the Beastly Mutation (4) Dread Power, representing their razor wings. Furthermore, they are incapable of producing any vocal sound.<br /> <br /> Torch-born: the Mockeries of the Frankenstein are fascinated by fire, and enjoy nothing more than Promethean flesh burnt to a crisp.<br /> All Torch-born gain the Crucible of Flesh (4) Dread Power (see below).When noticing a fire the size of a campfire or larger, the Torch-born must succeed on a Resolve+Composure roll penalized by the size of the fire or spend the rest of the scene staring at it in adoration, unless disturbed before the scene ends.<br /> <br /> New Dread Powers:<br /> <br /> Crucible of Flesh:<br /> Cost: 1 Pyros<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Presence+Occult<br /> Effect: the Pandoran inflicts 1 point of lethal damage to any creature in contact with it as its flesh becomes intensely hot to the touch. Alternatively, this power sets fire to any flammable material the pandoran is in contact with.<br /> <br /> Inertia:<br /> Cost: 1 Pyros<br /> Action: Extended (Target number = Azoth, each roll represents one turn of effort)<br /> Dice Pool: Wits+Occult<br /> Effect: once successful this Dread Power cancels the effect of one specific Transmutation, and prevents the Transmutation from being used again during the rest of the scene. This Dread Power can only be used once per scene on a single Promethean.<br /> <br /> Any feedback welcome!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}